userStories.description:
**Goal** — Preserve the shared token estimator in a leaf utility, delete the optimizer subsystem/API and explicitly reject plugins declaring its removed extension. **Motivation** — `src/optimizer/` (`resolveOptimizer`, `NoopOptimizer`) was consumed only by the optimizer stage B2b-1 deleted. **Approach** — Design Part 4: the prompt optimizer. Source paths below are relative to `packages/nax/src/`. `estimateTokens` moves, unchanged, to a new leaf module:

```typescript
// src/utils/tokens.ts
/**
 * Estimate token count using simple heuristic. * ~4 chars per token for English text (rough estimate). */
export function estimateTokens(text: string): number {
  return Math.ceil(text.length / 4);
}
```

`src/utils/` has no barrel; its modules are imported by path (`../utils/json-file`, `@/utils/git`), and `utils/tokens.ts` follows that. | Site | After |
|:---|:---|
| `context/builder.ts:12`, `context/elements.ts:8`, `constitution/loader.ts:11` | import `estimateTokens` from `../utils/tokens` |
| `context/fragments/store.ts:25`, `context/test-scanner/index.ts:14`, `context/rules/rule-sections/index.ts:21`, `context/engine/providers/static-rules.ts:28`, `context/engine/providers/static-rules-budget-notice.ts:13` | import `estimateTokens` from `@/utils/tokens` |
| `context/index.ts:5`, `constitution/index.ts:9` | re-export `estimateTokens` from `../utils/tokens` |
| `plugins/types.ts:9` | the `IPromptOptimizer` import goes |
| `plugins/types.ts:49` | `"optimizer"` leaves the `PluginType` union |
| `plugins/types.ts:127-128` | `PluginExtensions.optimizer` and its doc comment go |
| `plugins/types.ts:163-175` | the "Optimizer Extension" section header and the optimizer type re-export go |
| `plugins/index.ts:23`, `:29`, `:42-43` | the comment and the `IPromptOptimizer`, `PromptOptimizerInput` and `PromptOptimizerResult` re-exports go |
| `plugins/registry.ts:18`, `:206-216` | the `IPromptOptimizer` import and `getOptimizers()` with its doc comment go |
| `plugins/validator.ts:24`, `:129-130`, `:153-176` | `"optimizer"` leaves `VALID_PLUGIN_TYPES`; the `"optimizer"` case and `validateOptimizer` go |
| `plugins/validator.ts` | new: `removedOptimizerMessage(pluginName)` exported, and a check in `validatePlugin`, after the `provides` array is validated as non-empty and before each entry is checked against `VALID_PLUGIN_TYPES`, that returns `null` after a `warn` on stage `"plugins"` with `removedOptimizerMessage(plugin.name)` when `provides` includes `"optimizer"` |

The new validator code:

```typescript
/** Extension type removed with pipeline mode; a plugin still declaring it fails validation by name. */
const REMOVED_OPTIMIZER_TYPE = "optimizer";

/** Warning for a plugin that still declares the removed optimizer extension. */
export function removedOptimizerMessage(pluginName: string): string {
  return `Plugin '${pluginName}' validation failed: the 'optimizer' extension was removed with pipeline mode; remove it from 'provides'`;
}

// in validatePlugin, after the non-empty `provides` check:
if (plugin.provides.includes(REMOVED_OPTIMIZER_TYPE)) {
  getSafeLogger()?.warn("plugins", removedOptimizerMessage(plugin.name));
  return null;
}
```

A `null` from `validatePlugin` already makes the loader skip the plugin with its existing `Plugin validation failed for '<path>'` warning (`plugins/loader.ts:449-455`). A plugin that carries `extensions.optimizer` without listing `"optimizer"` in `provides` is unaffected: extensions not named in `provides` were already ignored. Deleted: `optimizer/index.ts`, `optimizer/noop.optimizer.ts`, `optimizer/types.ts` (the whole directory). The plugin tests that use `optimizer` as their sample extension (`registry.test.ts`, `plugins-registry.test.ts`, `validator.test.ts`, `loader.test.ts`, `config-resolution.test.ts`, `config-integration.test.ts`, `runner-config-plugins.test.ts`, `cli-plugins.test.ts`) switch those fixtures to the `reporter` extension (an object with a `name` string, which `validateReporter` requires) and keep their assertions about loading, ordering, config resolution and listing. **Scope** — In: estimator implementation/imports/re-exports, optimizer plugin types/registry/validator removals, named rejection, reporter fixture migrations and optimizer test-helper cleanup. Delete test/unit/optimizer/index.test.ts and test/helpers/optimizer-result.ts; remove makeOptimizerResult from helpers/index.ts and getOptimizers from helpers/plugin-registry.ts; remove only optimizer-specific assertions in retained plugin tests. Out: US-005's mutation subsystem and US-006's other orphans. Keep loader allowed-root/security checks unchanged. Config keys and their schemas, defaults, merge handling, migrations and descriptions: `optimizer.*` (with the `_applyRemovedOptimizerKeysShim` shim), `prompts.overrides` (with `PROMPT_OVERRIDE_ROLES`, the precheck override-file warning in `precheck/checks-warnings.ts` and the `prompts.overrides` lines in `cli/config-display.ts` and `cli/config-descriptions.ts`), `execution.mutationCheck` and the `advisor.callers` flags; wave B3 decides them. Docs and package context files that describe `nax prompts`, prompt overrides, `IPromptOptimizer`, `src/optimizer/` or mutation testing (`docs/guides/prompt-customization.md`, `docs/guides/cli-reference.md`, the `.nax/context.md` files and the `CLAUDE.md` / `AGENTS.md` files generated from them); `.nax/` is read-only to the run, so they are updated in wave B4. Stage/role registry strings also remain B3 work; the PluginType and validator entries explicitly named above are in scope here. Do not consolidate unrelated private estimator functions or create a utils barrel. **Interface** — `validatePlugin(module: unknown): NaxPlugin | null` (`plugins/validator.ts:42`). Target: same signature; returns `null` for a plugin whose `provides` includes `"optimizer"`, after a `warn` with `removedOptimizerMessage(name)`. `PluginType` (`plugins/types.ts:48`). Target: `"router" | "agent" | "reviewer" | "context-provider" | "reporter" | "post-run-action" | "loop-handlers" | "resources"`. `PluginRegistry` (`plugins/registry.ts`). Target: no `getOptimizers()` method; every other method unchanged. `estimateTokens(text: string): number`. Target: declared in `utils/tokens.ts`; `@/context` and `@/constitution` re-export it from there. **Verification** — Create only the utility and `packages/nax/test/unit/utils/tokens.test.ts`; test the direct heuristic and identity of both barrel re-exports. Add legacy-only and mixed optimizer/reporter rejection plus unchanged reporter identity assertions through `validatePlugin` imported from `@/plugins`, using the exact exported message from validator.ts and a restored logger fixture. In the existing loader integration tests, create real plugin modules for optimizer and reporter, disable `nax-curator` and `nax-auto-pr` through disabledPlugins, assert the registry contains only the reporter and the error sink receives the existing validation-failed warning; reset the sink afterward. Retain generic fixture loading/order/config/listing assertions after migration.

Verification, run in packages/nax, after the story's changes: (1) `bun run typecheck`; a missed reference or a barrel re-exporting a deleted module or name fails here. (2) A path sweep: for each source file this story deletes, with `<stem>` its path below `src/` without the extension, run `rg -n --fixed-strings '<stem>' src bin test scripts ../repo-tooling/scripts ../repo-tooling/test`, and the same for each deleted test file's path below `test/`. Expected: zero hits, else stop. A hit in code, in a test that reads a source file by path, or in a path list a test or script iterates is a missed reference. A hit in a comment is a stale comment and is reworded, in any file (a comment edit needs no Modifies entry). Known comment hits for this story's stems, reworded rather than a stop: `plugins/extensions.ts:145`. For `src/optimizer/` as a whole the sweep patterns are `@/optimizer`, `/optimizer"` and `optimizer/types`. Expected and not a stop: hits in `scripts/baselines/*.json`, which step 3 clears; the historical note in `../repo-tooling/scripts/check-coverage.ts:103`; the `stage-assembler-scope-files.test.ts` fixture string in `../repo-tooling/test/unit/scripts/check-test-satellites.test.ts:17`, which tests a file-name classifier; the stale `test/unit/acceptance/generator-*.test.ts` entries in `scripts/check-inline-test-mocks.ts` (`:48`, `:78`, `:139`, `:140`), which name test files earlier waves deleted; and the config keys, selectors and registry strings Out of Scope leaves to wave B3 (`optimizer`, `prompts.overrides`, `mutationCheck`, the `"prompt"` and `"optimizer"` stage names). A longer sibling stem that shares the prefix is not a hit when that sibling is deleted too or is a deleted test. Line numbers are at `c3266de8a`; when an earlier story edited the same file, locate each site by its symbol or test name. (3) `bun run check:complexity:update`, and `bun run check:file-sizes -- --update-baseline` when that check reports a lowerable entry; `check:complexity` fails with "baseline is stale" while a deleted file or function is still listed. After `check:all` is green, `bun run check:test-escape-hatches:update`. Do not edit `scripts/baselines/coverage-per-file-baseline.json` (no deleted file has an entry). (4) `bun run check:all` and `bun run test`. A trimmed source file also drops the imports only its removed declarations used; biome's noUnusedImports reports them.
